            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0341" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.51/212</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Belden to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 12. Minister of Finance resumed duties a few days ago. Great reserve
                    regarding loan negotiations is maintained.</p>
                <p>Without definite information, I am inclined to think it is the intention of the
                    Government to present to Congress a proposal for a loan of $25,000,000 to pay
                    internal debt and purchase of railway bonds. Am endeavoring to obtain
                    information of a more definite character. Norton arrives to-morrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belden</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
